From 7f40509578d26ec0384652b9064d53be58ad660b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephenuffugus <99242197+Stephenuffugus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 05:28:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] The hunt can finally win: capture rework, real fleets,
 tongue + burrow, and bridges over the river
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The July playtest verdict was 'capture still not really possible', and the
code agreed — four separate mechanisms each guaranteed a walking player
could never be abducted:

1. BEAM_TRACK_SPD sat below walk speed at every difficulty, so holding the
   stick outran the beam forever. Now the beam GRIPS (speed × 1−0.6·charge)
   and tracks at 118/155/180.
2. steer()'s arrival damping made a chasing ship SLOWER than a walking
   player inside ~48px — it could hover at 40px forever and never reach
   beam range (26). Pursuit steering now skips the arrive slowdown and
   turns twice as sharply (no more orbiting the runner).
3. Charge only built inside 26px and DRAINED in the 26–64 band, so every
   wiggle reset the ratchet. A still-locked beam now holds its charge, and
   the break ring + LoS grace scale with charge: a fresh lock slips like
   before, a half-charged one has to be beaten with a real tool.
4. Crossing one tree cell zeroed the pursuit: signal died at the SCAN_R
   line mid-chase and suspicion decayed to give-up in under a second.
   Chasing hunters now sense on a 1.75× leash and their suspicion fades
   at 0.35× while committed. Blatant signals (≥0.55) escalate at double
   speed — a hunter passing over an unmatched runner does not ponder.

Fairness kept: charge scales DOWN against a fading target, so freeze+match
under the beam is a winnable race; a matched hider (C≤0.3) can never trip
the blatant escalation; EASY beams remain walk-out-able for kids.

MANY more hunters searching (the other half of the note): fleets are now
2/4/6 (+1 on big maps, heat cap 8) and the separation spread runs at every
difficulty, so patrols fan out instead of clumping.

Two new abilities (the counterplay for the meaner beam): TONGUE (B) zips
you to the nearest cover anchor, aimable with the stick — out-ranges any
beam ring; BURROW (X) sinks you into soft ground for 2.5s, only your eyes
showing (the favicon, playable), refused mid-grip and on hard ground.

Jessie's river rule on riverline: the two concrete causeways DAMMED the
river — there was no 'under the bridge' to swim. They are now real decks:
water flows beneath, a new 'bridge' cover type roofs the crossing (blocks
LoS including the endpoint cell), the deck draws over the swimmer with
your eyes glinting through, and the level editor + map validator know the
type. Swim the water line and the bridge shelters the crossing.

Verified: full headless suite green (smoke/survive/abilities/hunt/
timeattack/math/twotone/pass8/controls/lockandlook/progression/maps/tour/
online) plus the new capture suite — 19 assertions, 4 consecutive clean
runs. Abduction of a fleeing exposed runner: ~7 simulated seconds.

